  "methodLimits": [
    "Sequential single A/B pair, without randomized repeated trials or fixed delivered fragment/presentation rates; QEMU adapts encoding automatically.",
    "Display intervals differ and are best-effort actor samples. Each rate uses its own actual interval; CPU uses paired same-host monotonic counters. CPU intervals lie inside the longer Display windows, with different endpoints.",
    "An explicit 30-second warmup wait does not imply identical observation times; actual warmups and finite-fixture end ages are recorded.",
    "Cumulative timing percentiles/maxima are not subtracted. Batch receive-to-ready/publisher timing samples one representative member per revision and is not directly comparable to the control per-fragment population.",
    "Native counts mean accepted fragments in both builds. Metal presentations may contain partial updates; no complete-frame FPS or per-key input-to-photon gain is inferred.",
    "The advanced-video CPU fallback field and MJPEG decoder Data-storage fallback do not enumerate all MJPEG composition fallbacks. The residual decoded-minus-native gap remains unclassified.",
    "Copy bytes are accounted canonical work, not measured hardware bandwidth utilization; copy waits include GPU queue/completion and actor resumption.",
    "Pool exhaustion is counted per checkout attempt; a failed batch can affect several fragments. Readback rate increased, and the approximate native/decoded ratio fell; these remain concerns.",
    "Process memory endpoints are gauges after different warmups, not peak-memory acceptance."
